        "ParentObjectID": "fl_ancient_cairn",
        "LocalizationKey": "Forest_Lore_AncientCairn_CardDescription",
        "DefaultText": "A long mound of grey stones under the oaks, grown over with grass and bramble. Someone was laid in it long before anyone now living came to this forest, and the stones were heaped high so that they would stay. The mouth of the tomb faces the morning sun. Once its goods are taken, the cairn stands open and quiet, and it does not fill again."
    },
